      "content": "Taking leftover antibiotics without a prescription is dangerous because they may not target your specific infection, leading to treatment failure or severe complications like bacterial pneumonia. You should never use antibiotics just to \"test\" shutdown an existing infection or cover your tracks; this behavior directly contributes to antibiotic resistance. Given your symptoms involving a high fever and severe pain, or if you become significantly more concerned about potential complications, it is crucial that you make an appointment with a healthcare provider for proper diagnosis.",
