      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Completing a full course of antibiotics for a new, unverified infection is unsafe because dosing schedules and drug combinations change based on the specific bacteria causing your current illness. Even if you think it will work, the residues may not be the correct amount or type needed to treat your specific throat infection, which could leave you worse off or cause side effects you don't want. Ultimately, it is never okay to self-prescribe antibiotics, especially for things that could become serious like strep throat, and you need to consult a doctor to get the right medication safely.",
      "source": "target",
